{%- doc -%}
  Builds the class list for a ../design-system/src/react/Button/Button.tsx button. Extracted from
  blocks/mionas-button.liquid so that block is not the only place the vocabulary is spelled out:
  blocks/mionas-add-to-cart.liquid needs the same classes on a <button> it cannot render itself, and
  used to rebuild the same `mionas-button--<variant>` string by hand -- two copies that had to be
  kept in step, and would silently diverge the moment a variant or size was added.

  IT EMITS CLASSES, NOT AN ELEMENT, and that is the most it can share. The add-to-cart button's
  markup has to come from snippets/add-to-cart-button.liquid: that snippet is the
  <add-to-cart-component> wrapper, the ref="addToCartButton" binding and the checkmark-burst spans
  that drive the added-to-cart animation and the fly-to-cart flight. There is nothing to parameterise
  there -- a shared element snippet would have to emit an <a>, a submit <button> and a
  quick-add <button> with on:click, which is three elements wearing one name.

  THE CSS THESE CLASSES NEED LIVES IN THIS SNIPPET'S STYLESHEET TAG, and every file that wears the
  classes must build them here. Shopify ships only the stylesheet CSS of files a page renders. The
  rules used to sit in blocks/mionas-button.liquid, and blocks/mionas-add-to-cart.liquid wears the
  classes without rendering that block, so a collection page shipped the add-to-cart button with no
  Mionas rules at all ("Full width does nothing"). Keep every .mionas-button rule in this one sheet:
  split across two, their relative order would decide every tie between them.

  @param {string} [variant] - primary, secondary, outline, ghost, danger, inverse-primary or inverse-ghost. Anything else falls back to primary.
  @param {string} [size] - sm, md or lg. Defaults to md, which adds no modifier because .mionas-button carries the md metrics itself.
  @param {boolean} [full_width] - Adds the --full modifier.
  @param {string} [prefix] - Classes to put in front, for a caller's own hooks (e.g. add-to-cart-button, which Horizon's animation CSS hangs off).

  @example
  {%- capture button_classes -%}
    {%- render 'mionas-button-class', variant: 'primary', size: 'md', full_width: true -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  comment
    Whitelisted rather than interpolated: an unrecognised value would silently emit a modifier class
    that no rule matches, producing a button with no colour at all -- harder to spot than an
    obviously wrong one. Same pattern as the role whitelist in snippets/mionas-text.liquid; keep both
    lists in step with the stylesheet below.
  endcomment
  assign allowed_variants = 'primary|secondary|outline|ghost|danger|inverse-primary|inverse-ghost' | split: '|'
  assign resolved_variant = variant | default: 'primary'
  unless allowed_variants contains resolved_variant
    assign resolved_variant = 'primary'
  endunless

  assign allowed_sizes = 'sm|md|lg' | split: '|'
  assign resolved_size = size | default: 'md'
  unless allowed_sizes contains resolved_size
    assign resolved_size = 'md'
  endunless

  assign classes = 'mionas-button mionas-button--' | append: resolved_variant

  comment
    md adds no modifier: .mionas-button already carries the md height, padding and font-size, so a
    --md class would have nothing to declare.
  endcomment
  unless resolved_size == 'md'
    assign classes = classes | append: ' mionas-button--' | append: resolved_size
  endunless

  if full_width
    assign classes = classes | append: ' mionas-button--full'
  endif

  if prefix != blank
    assign classes = prefix | append: ' ' | append: classes
  endif
-%}
{{- classes -}}

{% stylesheet %}
  .mionas-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--button-base-gap);
    border: 1.5px solid transparent;
    border-radius: var(--button-base-radius);
    font-family: var(--button-base-font-family);
    font-weight: var(--button-base-font-weight);
    cursor: pointer;
    white-space: nowrap;
    text-decoration: none;
    height: var(--button-size-md-height);
    padding: 0 var(--button-size-md-padding);
    font-size: var(--button-size-md-font-size);
  }

  .mionas-button--sm {
    height: var(--button-size-sm-height);
    padding: 0 var(--button-size-sm-padding);
    font-size: var(--button-size-sm-font-size);
  }

  .mionas-button--sm .mionas-button__icon {
    width: var(--button-size-sm-icon-size);
    height: var(--button-size-sm-icon-size);
  }

  .mionas-button--lg {
    height: var(--button-size-lg-height);
    padding: 0 var(--button-size-lg-padding);
    font-size: var(--button-size-lg-font-size);
  }

  .mionas-button--lg .mionas-button__icon {
    width: var(--button-size-lg-icon-size);
    height: var(--button-size-lg-icon-size);
  }

  /* Button.tsx has no fullWidth prop -- the prototype's `full-width` was its own harness prop.
     The Contacto page needs a full-width WhatsApp button, so this is a theme-side addition;
     see the spec's follow-ups about proposing it back to the design system.

     THE SELECTOR IS DOUBLED ON PURPOSE AND MUST NOT BE FLATTENED BACK TO .mionas-button--full.
     base.css:1006-1040 declares `.button { display: grid; width: fit-content }`, and a Mionas button
     can carry that class: snippets/add-to-cart-button.liquid prefixes whatever class attribute it is
     handed with a literal "button", so every product-card add-to-cart button wears both. At one
     class each, `fit-content` and `width: 100%` tie on specificity and only source order separates
     them -- and `fit-content` is precisely the "full width does nothing" symptom. Source order
     favours this file today, but an order-dependent tie is not a win, so the double class settles it
     at (0,2,0).

     `display` is doubled for the same reason: it ties with .button's `grid`. */
  .mionas-button.mionas-button--full {
    display: flex;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .mionas-button--primary {
    background: var(--button-primary-background);
    color: var(--button-primary-foreground);
  }

  .mionas-button--secondary {
    background: var(--button-secondary-background);
    color: var(--button-secondary-foreground);
  }

  .mionas-button--outline {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--button-outline-foreground);
    box-shadow: var(--button-outline-shadow);
  }

  .mionas-button--ghost {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--button-ghost-foreground);
  }

  .mionas-button--danger {
    background: var(--button-danger-background);
    color: var(--button-danger-foreground);
  }

  .mionas-button--inverse-primary {
    background: var(--button-inverse-primary-background);
    color: var(--button-inverse-primary-foreground);
  }

  .mionas-button--inverse-ghost {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--button-inverse-ghost-foreground);
  }

  .mionas-button[aria-disabled="true"] {
    opacity: var(--button-state-disabled-opacity);
    cursor: default;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .mionas-button:active {
    transform: scale(var(--button-state-pressed-scale));
    opacity: var(--button-state-pressed-opacity);
  }

  .mionas-button__icon {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex: none;
    width: var(--button-size-md-icon-size);
    height: var(--button-size-md-icon-size);
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
